Shaun,

Note this is not an advertisement, but I just wanted to give you some insight into what is being used in Texas.

You might check out schnuppconsulting.com <http://schnuppconsulting.com>.  They have information on a wildlife research database that can be used for multi-species, distance sampling surveys, and is compatible with multiple platforms (handheld gps, smartphones, rangefinders, etc.).  It was developed by Matthew Schnupp (Wildlife Biologist for King Ranch) in partnership with Caesar Kleberg Wildlife Research Institute.  We have used it the last 3 years for helicopter-based, distance sampling surveys for bobwhites, as well as multi-species ungulate surveys.  Our equipment set up utilizes a Trimble Juno 5b handheld and 2-Trimble Laser Ace 1000 rangefinders that are connected via bluetooth.

Best,

John

